From: John Morkel <john@morkel.me>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:02:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: airoha,en7581-eth: add a PON mode for GMAC port 2

On the EN7581 the second GMAC port can carry the SoC's PON MAC (GPON
or XGS-PON) instead of an Ethernet MAC. The port then has no PHY and no
PCS: a PON MAC driver owns the link, and it decides which GEM port and
T-CONT each frame uses. Add the boolean airoha,pon to a GMAC port node to
select that mode, and allow it on port 2 only.

Signed-off-by: John Morkel <john@morkel.me>
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/airoha,en7581-eth.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/airoha,en7581-eth.yaml
index 6d22131..ba01feb 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/airoha,en7581-eth.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/airoha,en7581-eth.yaml
@@ -97,10 +97,28 @@ patternProperties:
         maximum: 4
         description: GMAC port identifier
 
+      airoha,pon:
+        type: boolean
+        description:
+          The port is the SoC's PON interface (GPON or XGS-PON) rather than
+          an Ethernet MAC. It has no PHY and no PCS, so the port takes no
+          phy-mode, phy-handle, pcs-handle or fixed-link. A PON MAC driver
+          owns its link state and maps its traffic to GEM ports and T-CONTs
+          through the frame engine driver. Only GMAC port 2 can be the PON
+          interface.
+
     required:
       - reg
       - compatible
 
+    if:
+      required:
+        - airoha,pon
+    then:
+      properties:
+        reg:
+          const: 2
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
@@ -162,5 +180,11 @@ examples:
           compatible = "airoha,eth-mac";
           reg = <1>;
         };
+
+        pon: ethernet@2 {
+          compatible = "airoha,eth-mac";
+          reg = <2>;
+          airoha,pon;
+        };
       };
     };
